message: "If you use this code or data, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "sycophancy-eval: social pressure and induced Big Five personas in frontier language models"
authors:
  - family-names: Hunalp
    given-names: Berfay
    affiliation: "Independent researcher, Nice, France"
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-16"
repository-code: "https://github.com/BerfayHunalp/sycophancy-eval"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - sycophancy
  - large language models
  - Big Five
  - Agreeableness
  - trait activation
  - pre-registration
abstract: >-
  Pre-registered 3 x 5 within-item experiment on Claude Sonnet 5 and GPT-5.2:
  three social-pressure conditions (control, polite disagreement, authority
  claim) crossed with five system-prompt personas (none, high/low Agreeableness,
  high/low Conscientiousness) on 100 MMLU items. Includes all prompts, raw
  responses, IPIP-50 manipulation check, human norms and analysis code.
